🔧 conveyor fix — finding NOT reproduced on head `dfa0b5c` (already fixed; stale referral)

**Not reproduced.** The 22:34 finding is word-for-word the 19:51 finding (`glance-mount.ts:113`, `state.data.agents[deep.agent]`). It was posted against head `dfa0b5c7`, but that head contains no such expression: `git grep -n 'agents\[deep' dfa0b5c` returns nothing across the whole tree (source, tests, e2e, comments). The 21:52 fix comment on this PR already addressed it.

**Actual lines 113–116 at `dfa0b5c`:**
```ts
if (deep.agent) {
  // own keys only: ?agent=constructor / __proto__ / toString is no session
  if (Object.hasOwn(state.data.agents, deep.agent)) { if (!agentOpened) { agentOpened = true; agent = deep.agent; } }
  else notes.push(`No agent panel for session "${deep.agent}" ...`);
}
```

**Check run today on this head:** `glance-deeplink.test.ts` — 18 passed (18), including the 7 inherited-name cases (`constructor`, `__proto__`, `toString`, `hasOwnProperty`, `valueOf`, `isPrototypeOf`, `__defineGetter__`) → note shown, no panel, no throw.

**No new commit / push:** nothing to repair; head stays `dfa0b5c`. Re-arming so an independent review judges the current code.

**Variants considered:** unchanged from the 21:52 round. The only URL-keyed lookup is the one above (`Object.hasOwn`); `?card=` compares refs with no key lookup; `glance-view.ts` `agents[st.agent]` is reached only via the validated `deep.agent` or a click on a rendered own key (`data-arg`). Matrix: untrusted text — fixed at `glance-mount.ts:115`; all other rows n/a.
